[00:09.57]Why was the Ambassador particularly lucky? | 为什么大使特别幸运？
[00:14.92]When the Ambassador of Escalopia returned home for lunch, his wife got a shock. | 当艾斯卡罗比亚大使回家吃午饭时，把妻子吓了一跳。
[00:23.22]He looked pale and his clothes were in a frightful state. | 他面色苍白，衣服也糟糕透了。
[00:28.74]'What has happened?' she asked. | “出什么事了？”她问。
[00:32.77]'How did your clothes get into such a mess?' | “你的衣服怎么弄成这个样子？”
[00:37.81]'A fire extinguisher, my dear,' answered the Ambassador drily. | “灭火器干的好事，亲爱的，”大使冷冰冰地回答说。
[00:43.66]'University students set the Embassy on fire this morning.' | “今天上午，大学生们放火烧了大使馆。”
[00:48.63]'Good heavens!' exclaimed his wife. | “天哪！”他的妻子惊叫道。
[00:52.87]'And where were you at the time?' | “当时你在哪儿？”
[00:56.61]'I was in my office as usual,' answered the Ambassador. | “我和往常一样，在办公室里，”大使回答说。
[01:01.45]'The fire broke out in the basement. | “火是在地下室烧起来的，
[01:04.41]I went down immediately, of course, and that fool, Horst, | 我立刻就下去了，当然，那个傻瓜霍斯特
[01:09.87]aimed a fire extinguisher at me. | 拿着灭火器对准了我。
[01:12.80]He thought I was on fire. | 他以为我身上着火了。
[01:15.67]I must definitely get that fellow posted.' | 我一定要把那个家伙调走。”
[01:20.33]The Ambassador's wife went on asking questions, | 大使夫人继续提出问题，
[01:24.40]when she suddenly noticed a big hole in her husband's hat. | 这时她突然发现丈夫的帽子上有个洞。
[01:30.27]'And how can you explain that?' she asked. | “那么这又如何解释呢？”她问。
[01:34.88]'Oh, that,' said the Ambassador. | “哦，那个啊，”大使说。
[01:38.56]'Someone fired a shot through my office window. | “有人从我办公室的窗户开了一枪。
[01:42.59]Accurate, don't you think? | 打得很准，是不是？
[01:44.88]Fortunately, I wasn't wearing it at the time. | 幸运的是，我当时没戴着它。
[01:49.36]If I had been, I would not have been able to get home for lunch.' | 如果我当时戴着的话，现在就不能回家吃午饭了。”
